When for_each is used in two resource give reference like shown below

service_account = google_service_account.service_account["composer_sa"].email

Note: Here composer_sa is input key resource in dev.tfvars  

Ex:

service_accounts = {
  composer_sa = {
    composer_service_account = "composer-sa"
    display_name             = "This service is using for test composer"
  }
}
------
GitHub is rolling out an update to its Ubuntu-latest tag for hosted runners. This update introduces a significant change that requires your immediate attention to avoid pipeline disruptions.
 
What’s Changing?
Starting December 5, 2024, GitHub will begin transitioning the Ubuntu-latest tag to point to Ubuntu 24.04.
Terraform is no longer pre-installed in the new Ubuntu 24.04 image.
This transition will be complete by January 17, 2025.
 
How Does This Impact Us?
Many of our GitHub workflows currently use the Ubuntu-latest tag.
Pipelines depending on Terraform will fail unless Terraform is explicitly installed.
 
Steps to Prevent Pipeline Failures
To ensure a smooth transition, update your pipelines as follows:
Add Terraform Installation Step: Include the following step before the Terraform init step in your pipeline:
- name: Terraform Installation
   uses: hashicorp/setup-terraform@v3
   with:
      terraform_wrapper: false
 
 
